*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*%
*% Filterless pass-through PPD for HP DesignJet 1050C. Apple's CUPS build
*% removed support for the classic "-m raw" queue model, so this PPD
*% stands in for it: *cupsFilter2's filter field of "-" tells CUPS no
*% conversion is needed - the submitted file (an HP-GL/2 .plt/.hpgl
*% export from CAD software) is sent to the socket backend byte-for-byte.
*% This is the plotter's native vector language: no rasterization,
*% smaller jobs, sharper lines than the general rastertohpgl2rtl queue.
*%
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.2.2"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "HPDJRAW.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "HP"
*Product: "(DesignJet 1050C)"
*ModelName: "HP DesignJet 1050C Raw HPGL2 Passthrough"
*ShortNickName: "HP DesignJet 1050C Raw"
*NickName: "HP DesignJet 1050C, Raw HP-GL/2 Passthrough"
*PSVersion: "(none) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "0"
*ColorDevice: True
*DefaultColorSpace: RGB
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*TTRasterizer: None
*cupsVersion: 2.3
*cupsManualCopies: True
*cupsModelNumber: 1051
*cupsFilter2: "application/octet-stream application/octet-stream 0 -"
*cupsFilter2: "text/plain application/octet-stream 0 -"

*OpenUI *PageSize/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: ARCHD
*PageSize ARCHD/Arch D 24x36in (set by the HPGL2 file itself): ""
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: ARCHD
*PageRegion ARCHD/Arch D 24x36in (set by the HPGL2 file itself): ""
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*DefaultPaperDimension: ARCHD
*PaperDimension ARCHD/Arch D 24x36in (set by the HPGL2 file itself): "1728 2592"

*DefaultImageableArea: ARCHD
*ImageableArea ARCHD/Arch D 24x36in (set by the HPGL2 file itself): "0 0 1728 2592"

*%End of PPD file.
